* LX - RUN A PROGRAM FROM AN LBR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* LX - RUN A PROGRAM FROM AN LBR

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:LX [-[dir:]library] command-line

Finds and runs a COM member from a command library. Without an explicit
library it uses its configured command libraries/search rules.

Running a member executes code, unlike listing with LDIR. Inspect the
source and origin of the library first. This launcher remains private and
does not bypass BYE caller execution rules.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
